  "format": "kshader",
  "generator": "Kekenik Shader",
  "graph": {
    "comments": [
      {
        "color": "#60a5fa",
        "id": "note_time",
        "position": {
          "x": 22,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 39,
          "w": 1068
        },
        "text": "Time, the world-space position (ripples and foam are laid out in world XZ so they do not swim with the mesh) and the world normal / view direction."
      },
      {
        "color": "#60a5fa",
        "id": "note_waves",
        "position": {
          "x": 1294,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 39,
          "w": 2072
        },
        "text": "Three **Gerstner wave** kits with different directions, wavelengths (×1, ×0.55, ×0.3) and steepness (×0.5, ×0.3, ×0.2 of the total, so crests never loop). Offsets add to the position; the normal deltas add to `(0,1,0)` and are normalised."
      },
      {
        "color": "#22d3ee",
        "id": "note_ripple",
        "position": {
          "x": 1294,
          "y": 1341
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 39,
          "w": 1460
        },
        "text": "The **Flow Map Sample** kit advects the ripple normal map along the flow texture with two phase-shifted layers; the result is decoded and scaled. Coordinates are world XZ × tiling."
      },
      {
        "color": "#f87171",
        "id": "note_depth",
        "position": {
          "x": 3570,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 39,
          "w": 2378
        },
        "text": "Two **Depth Intersection** kits: one with the *Depth Range* gives the shallow→deep gradient, one with the *Foam Width* gives the shoreline mask `1 − fade`. A single value-noise evaluation breaks the foam line: `foam = smoothstep(0.45, 0.55, mask + (noise − 0.5) × 0.7)`."
      },
      {
        "color": "#a78bfa",
        "id": "note_refr",
        "position": {
          "x": 3570,
          "y": 948
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 56,
          "w": 848
        },
        "text": "**Distortion Offset** bends the screen UV by the ripple normal (view space), **Scene Color** reads the opaque scene there. The **Fresnel kit** adds the sky colour at grazing angles — a cheap stand-in for a reflection probe."
      },
      {
        "color": "#fb923c",
        "id": "note_mix",
        "position": {
          "x": 6152,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 39,
          "w": 1460
        },
        "text": "`water = lerp(shallow, deep, fade)`, tinted refraction replaces part of it near the shore, foam wins over everything. Smoothness drops under foam; alpha rises with depth and under foam."
      },
      {
        "color": "#4ade80",
        "id": "note_out",
        "position": {
          "x": 7816,
          "y": 34
        },
        "size": {
          "h": 90,
          "w": 300
        },
        "text": "Vertex: displaced position + wave normal. Fragment: colour, ripple normal, smoothness, sky reflection as emission, alpha."
      }
    ],
